  design.board_ports.AUD_SD: "`AUD_SD`, the amplifier enable, is always high."
  design.board_ports.LED[15:0]: "the 16-bit `LED` output, which the block leaves off"

reasons:
  c12_nexys_pwm_audio_top.contract.parameters.TIMEOUT_CYCLES: "The specification names this parameter but gives no default or range; a positive proposed default is used."
  c12_nexys_pwm_audio_top.contract.parameters.BUILD_STAMP: "The specification names this parameter but gives no default or range; zero is a neutral proposed default."
  c12_nexys_pwm_audio_top.contract.ports.CLK100MHZ: "The test-hook list requires this top-level board-clock port; the module clock contract binds it to clk_sys."
  c12_nexys_pwm_audio_top.contract.ports.CPU_RESETN: "The test-hook list requires this top-level reset port; rst_sys is derived from the board reset with asynchronous assertion and synchronized release."
  c12_nexys_pwm_audio_top.contract.ports.rst: "The module reset input is the derived active-low reset distributed to the design."
  c12_nexys_pwm_audio_top.contract.ports.AUD_PWM: "The board-facing output must support high-impedance behavior, so the board port is declared open-drain."
  c12_nexys_pwm_audio_top.contract.registers: "The shell owns a 0x80-0xFF window; window_base 0x00 uses the beginning of that window. Relative register offsets are proposed in assumption A-2."
  design.clocks.clk_sys: "The named board clock is used directly; the specification sets the timing target at 100 MHz."
